  "database": "rschema_0402",
  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0402' consists of 9 tables. The 'Department' table represents the departmental information, including the department address, ID, name, and phone number. The 'Patient' table holds patient-related data, including age, contact information, diagnosis description, gender, name, patient ID, and visit date. The 'Ward' table contains information about the ward, including the number of beds and ward level. The 'Registration_Category' table contains registration category-related data, including the category ID and category name. The 'Medicine' table contains information about the medicines, including the barcode, medicine ID, name, price, and quantity. The 'Prescription' table holds prescription-related data, including the medicine information and prescription ID. The 'Doctor' table contains doctor-related data, including the date of birth, doctor ID, gender, name, title, work certificate, and years of employment. Finally, the 'Treatment' and 'Prescription_Medicine' tables reference the 'Patient' table, providing treatment content and prescription details respectively. All tables have primary keys and foreign keys to maintain entity integrity and referential integrity.\nThis schema is designed to manage various aspects of a hospital, including patient information, doctor details, medicine prescriptions, treatment plans, and departmental information. It allows for easy tracking and management of various aspects of the hospital's operations.",
  "gold_question": "System Description\nDescribes a hospital management system.\n\nMain functions of the system\n1. Doctor management: including basic information of doctors (name, gender, title, date of birth, years of employment, work permit).\n2. Department management: including basic information of departments (department name, personnel, department number, department phone number, department address).\n3. Patient management: including basic information of patients (name, gender, age, contact information, diagnosis description, date of consultation).\n4. Diagnosis and treatment management: including diagnosis and treatment information (case number, diagnosis and treatment content).\n5. Ward management: including basic information of wards (ward number, number of beds, ward level).\n6. Registration category management: including basic information of registration categories (category number, category name).\n7. Drug management: including basic information of drugs (name, quantity, price, barcode).\n8. Drug list management: including basic information of drug lists (drug list number, drug information).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0402.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0402\nCREATE TABLE `Department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Patient` (\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `diagnosis_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `visit_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patient_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Ward` (\n  `ward_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_beds` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ward_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ward_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Registration_Category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Medicine` (\n  `medicine_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `barcode` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`medicine_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Prescription` (\n  `prescription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`prescription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `prescription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `Patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Doctor` (\n  `doctor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `work_certificate` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `years_of_employment` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`doctor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Treatment` (\n  `treatment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `treatment_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`treatment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `treatment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `Patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Prescription_Medicine` (\n  `prescription_medicine_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `prescription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `medicine_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`prescription_medicine_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `prescription_medicine_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`prescription_id`) REFERENCES `Prescription` (`prescription_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescription_medicine_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`medicine_id`) REFERENCES `Medicine` (`medicine_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
